"A big earthquake releases a huge amount of energy.": "29a149a6edd1",
"A few minutes after an earthquake, the report appears on your phone. It might say: magnitude 6.5, depth 15 kilometers, intensity 5 Upper in Hualien, 4 in Taipei, 3 in Kaohsiung. That is a lot of numbers for one earthquake. Which one tells you how big it was?": "492b838e0bef",
"A few minutes after an earthquake, the report appears on your phone. It might say: magnitude 6.5, depth 15 kilometers, intensity 5 Upper in Hualien, 4 in Taipei, 3 in Kaohsiung. That is a lot of numbers for one earthquake. Which one tells you how big it was? The magnitude does. Magnitude tells how much energy the earthquake released where it started, deep underground. One earthquake has only one magnitude. It is the same number whether you are in Hualien, in Kaohsiung, or on the other side of the world. In Chinese, magnitude is written without the word for “level”: we say magnitude 6.5, and nothing more. The steps on the magnitude scale are huge. An earthquake of magnitude 6 releases about 32 times as much energy as one of magnitude 5. A magnitude 7 releases about 1,000 times as much. That is why a 7 is a disaster while a 5 may only rattle the windows. Intensity is different. It tells how hard the ground shook in one place. Close to the earthquake the shaking is strong, and farther away it is weaker. So one earthquake has many intensities, a different one for every town. Taiwan's scale has ten levels: 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 Lower, 5 Upper, 6 Lower, 6 Upper, and 7. Think of a light bulb. The bulb has one brightness, and that is like the magnitude. But how bright it looks depends on where you stand. Close to the bulb the light is strong, and across the room it is dim. That is like the intensity. Depth matters too. A shallow earthquake shakes the ground above it much harder than a deep one of the same magnitude. So when you read the next earthquake report, look at three things: the magnitude, the depth, and the intensity where you are. The last one tells you what your own house felt.": "9cba34f6c832",
